IdentityDocument: every form its examples take (area 19, "Changing a standard type's encoding")
encoding 1
column kind text
column country text
column number text
column expires date

example {"kind":"passport","country":"GB","number":"123456789","expires":"2030-01-31"}
text none
json {"kind":"passport","country":"GB","number":"123456789","expires":"2030-01-31"}
stored kind 'passport'
stored country 'GB'
stored number '123456789'
stored expires '2030-01-31'::date

example {"kind":"identity_card","country":"DE","number":"L01X00T47","expires":null}
text none
json {"kind":"identity_card","country":"DE","number":"L01X00T47","expires":null}
stored kind 'identity_card'
stored country 'DE'
stored number 'L01X00T47'
stored expires NULL::date
